          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"r2-api-use-case\">R2 API use case</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">In this notebook, we will show a simple use case involving interactions with\n R2 buckets associated to a Cloudflare account. This will involve the following:<br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">1. listing buckets;<br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">2. retrieving a file from a bucket.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Prerequisites:</strong><br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">- R2 API token (see <a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/api/s3/tokens/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> for info on how to create\n one);<br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">- An existing R2 bucket with a CORS policy (see\n <a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/buckets/cors/#add-cors-policies-from-the-dashboard\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>\n   how to configure).</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Note: on the CORS <code>AllowedOrigins</code> field, <code>http://localhost:8088</code> should be included.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "RGSE",
      "code_hash": "f32157b3805e9072f49565051ea5a673",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"listing-r2-buckets\">Listing R2 buckets</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">In order to get a list of R2 buckets, we can make use of the <code>/accounts/{account_id}/r2/buckets</code> endpoint.<br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Note: one call to this endpoint can return at most 1000 entries. Here we fetch only 100.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Hstk",
      "code_hash": "a45e51aeb3243260219002886586aeaa",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">We can then obtain extra info on each bucket by adding its name on the endpoint:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ZHCJ",
      "code_hash": "20843bb8706bd5e8e142e86d84c0b613",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The <code>storage_class</code> value is particularly important as bucket usage metrics may be separated between standard\nand infrequent access versions. For more information on storage classes, check the dedicated\n<a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/buckets/storage-classes/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">developers page</a>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Futher interactions with a given bucket can also be done using requests, but will require\n<a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_sigv-create-signed-request.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">signing</a>\neach request. We will download an object to memory as an example:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
